# Frontend Ticket Implementation Guide

This guide outlines how to integrate the backend ticket system into your frontend application (React/Next.js).

## 1. Interfaces (DTOs)

Define these TypeScript interfaces to match your backend data structures.

```typescript
// src/types/ticket.ts

export enum TicketStatus {
  VALID = 'VALID',
  USED = 'USED',
  EXPIRED = 'EXPIRED',
  CANCELLED = 'CANCELLED'
}

export interface Bundle {
  quantity: number;
  price: number; // Total price for the bundle
}

export interface TicketTypeDefinition {
  _id?: string; // Optional for creation
  name: string; // e.g., "Standard", "VIP"
  price: number;
  capacity: number;
  description?: string;
  bundles: Bundle[];
}

export interface Ticket {
  _id: string;
  ticketNumber: string;
  qrCode: string; // Base64 Data URL
  purchaseDate: string; // ISO Date
  tournament: string | { _id: string; name: string; startDate: string; endDate: string };
  user: string | { _id: string; username: string; email: string };
  type: string; // The NAME of the ticket type (e.g., "Standard")
  status: TicketStatus;
  price: number;
  usedAt?: string;
}

export interface CreateTicketDto {
  tournament: string; // Tournament ID
  user: string;       // User ID
  type: string;       // Ticket Type NAME (e.g., "Standard") - IMPORTANT: Send Name, NOT ID
  quantity: number;
  status?: TicketStatus;
}

export interface AddTicketTypesDto {
  ticketTypes: TicketTypeDefinition[];
}
```

---

## 2. API Service Methods

These functions handle communication with your backend endpoints.

```typescript
// src/services/ticketService.ts
import axios from 'axios';
import { CreateTicketDto, AddTicketTypesDto, Ticket } from '../types/ticket';

const API_URL = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL || 'http://localhost:3000';

// ==========================================
// FOR ORGANIZERS (Tournament Management)
// ==========================================

/**
 * Add or update ticket types for a tournament
 * Endpoint: POST /tournements/:id/tickets
 */
export const addTicketTypesToTournament = async (tournamentId: string, data: AddTicketTypesDto) => {
  const response = await axios.post(\`\${API_URL}/tournements/\${tournamentId}/tickets\`, data);
  return response.data;
};

// ==========================================
// FOR USERS (Booking Flow)
// ==========================================

/**
 * Get available ticket types for a specific tournament
 * Endpoint: GET /tournements/:id/available-tickets
 */
export const getAvailableTickets = async (tournamentId: string) => {
  const response = await axios.get(\`\${API_URL}/tournements/\${tournamentId}/available-tickets\`);
  // Returns: { tournament: {...}, availableTickets: [...] }
  return response.data;
};

/**
 * Book a ticket
 * Endpoint: POST /tickets
 */
export const bookTicket = async (ticketData: CreateTicketDto) => {
  const response = await axios.post(\`\${API_URL}/tickets\`, ticketData);
  return response.data; // Returns created tickets array
};

/**
 * Get current user's tickets
 * Endpoint: GET /tickets/my-tickets
 */
export const getMyTickets = async (userId: string) => {
  const response = await axios.get(\`\${API_URL}/tickets/my-tickets\`, {
    params: { userId }
  });
  return response.data;
};

/**
 * Get a specific ticket by ID
 */
export const getTicketById = async (ticketId: string) => {
  const response = await axios.get(\`\${API_URL}/tickets/\${ticketId}\`);
  return response.data;
};
```

---

## 3. Component Implementation Logic

### A. Organizer View: Adding Tickets to Tournament

Use this when creating or editing a tournament.

```javascript
/* Logic Snippet for "Add Ticket Type" Form */

const [ticketTypes, setTicketTypes] = useState([]);

const handleAddTicketType = () => {
  // Example data structure for a new type
  const newType = {
    name: "VIP",
    price: 150,
    capacity: 50,
    description: "VIP Access + Merch",
    bundles: [
      { quantity: 2, price: 280 } // Discounted bundle
    ]
  };
  
  // Add to local state first
  setTicketTypes([...ticketTypes, newType]);
};

const handleSaveToBackend = async () => {
  try {
    await addTicketTypesToTournament(tournamentId, { ticketTypes });
    alert("Ticket types saved successfully!");
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Failed to save ticket types", error);
  }
};
```

### B. User View: Booking a Ticket

1.  **Fetch Available Tickets**:
    Calls [getAvailableTickets(tournamentId)](file:///Users/khalilmouscou/Documents/_Esprit/projet%20Integr%C3%A9/Backend%20Nest/arena_chain/src/tournements/tournements.service.ts#265-309) on page load.
2.  **Select Type**:
    User selects a [TicketTypeDefinition](file:///Users/khalilmouscou/Documents/_Esprit/projet%20Integr%C3%A9/Backend%20Nest/arena_chain/src/tickets/schemas/ticket-type.schema.ts#16-42) (e.g., "Standard").
3.  **Determine Price**:
    *   Check if selected quantity matches a `bundle`.
    *   If yes, use `bundle.price`.
    *   If no, use `type.price * quantity`.
4.  **Submit Booking**:

```javascript
/* Logic Snippet for Booking Button */

const handleBookTicket = async () => {
  const bookingData = {
    tournament: tournamentId,
    user: currentUser._id,
    type: selectedType.name, // IMPORTANT: Send the NAME ("Standard"), not the ID
    quantity: selectedQuantity,
    status: 'VALID'
  };

  try {
    const tickets = await bookTicket(bookingData);
    // tickets[0].qrCode contains the QR code image data
    // Redirect to confirmation page or show modal
    router.push(\`/tickets/confirmation/\${tickets[0]._id}\`);
  } catch (error) {
    alert(error.response?.data?.message || "Booking failed");
  }
};
```

### C. Displaying the Ticket (QR Code)

The backend returns the QR code as a Base64 Data URI string. You can render it directly in an `<img>` tag.

```jsx
/* TicketDisplay Component */

const TicketDisplay = ({ ticket }) => {
  return (
    <div className="ticket-card">
      <h3>{ticket.type} Ticket</h3>
      <p>Tournament: {ticket.tournament.name}</p>
      
      <div className="qr-code-container">
        {/* Render Base64 QR Code directly */}
        <img src={ticket.qrCode} alt="Ticket QR Code" />
      </div>
      
      <p>Ticket #: {ticket.ticketNumber}</p>
    </div>
  );
};
```
